=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The reported overnight alert about R6 or R7 causing widespread middle-network failures is not substantiated by any live evidence. A topology-wide reachability sweep shows pc0 to pc12 and the reverse path both completing with 0% packet loss. Phase A infrastructure sweep found zero ACL drops, no addressing anomalies, no duplicate MACs, and all host routes intact. Phase B OSPF snapshot confirms both accused routers are fully operational: r6 holds three Full OSPF adjacencies in area 0.0.0.1 (with r4, r5, and r7) and carries 55 OSPF routes; r7 holds one Full adjacency with r6 (its only physical peer) and carries 57 OSPF routes. The TC snapshot shows clean pfifo_fast qdiscs with no shaping or corruption. Phase D pressure sweep found no stressed or resource-exhausted devices. Two longstanding anomalies appear in the snapshot — r8 has an orphaned OSPF area 0.0.0.2 with no peers, and r13 has its ospfd daemon absent — but both are chronic pre-existing conditions documented across multiple prior diagnostic sessions of this lab topology, neither lies on the pc0–pc12 forwarding path, and neither affects any observable traffic. The alarm was either a transient false positive that self-cleared, or was triggered by one of these pre-existing configuration artifacts rather than an acute failure. No corrective action is required for r6 or r7.
=== END ===